  [Escalation] Remediation options presented to manager:
    - Option 1 (Recommended): Distribute Demand Across an Additional Shift: Spread the 20% demand increment across a newly opened third shift so that each shift operates within current FatigueIndex (≤0.40) and Noise (≤80.0 dB) limits. No constraint values are relaxed. Approximately 12–18% of the incremental volume will be delivered one shift later than the original deadline, but all human-centric protections remain fully intact. Requires shift-supervisor sign-off and temporary staffing authorization.
      Preserves human constraints: Yes
    - Option 2 (Moderate): Deploy Noise Attenuation Controls and Relax FatigueIndex to 0.50: Install temporary acoustic enclosures and anti-vibration mounts to reduce equipment noise by an estimated 5–6 dB, bringing Noise back within the 80.0 dB limit. Simultaneously relax the FatigueIndex ceiling from 0.40 to 0.50 for a defined window (not to exceed 5 consecutive days), paired with mandatory 10-minute micro-breaks every 90 minutes and real-time wearable fatigue monitoring. This option meets approximately 90% of the demand increase within the original deadline. Requires written approval from the Safety Officer and must be reviewed daily.
      Preserves human constraints: No
    - Option 3 (Last Resort): Emergency Override — Relax Both Constraints with Enhanced Monitoring: Temporarily raise the FatigueIndex ceiling to 0.65 and the Noise ceiling to 85.0 dB for a strictly bounded emergency window (maximum 48 hours). Mandatory PPE (Class-E hearing protection), continuous biometric monitoring via wearables, and a dedicated safety observer on the floor are required at all times. All affected workers must provide informed consent and receive a compensatory rest period immediately following the window. This option meets 100% of demand within the original deadline but carries elevated occupational risk and must be authorized in writing by both the Plant Manager and the EHS Director before activation.
      Preserves human constraints: No

  [Manager] Decision: Option C
    Rationale: Prioritizing human well-being over deadline
